A1=Methods and quality checks
A2=Analysis definitions, provenance and limitations
A4=Topic | B4=Specification
A5=Endpoint | B5=Ψ (%) = 100 × I/(I+E) and Δ3 (%) = 100 × E/(I+E), using raw integrated band volumes from GelAnalyzer and the supplied band identities. No background re-estimation or fragment-length correction.
A6=Band roles | B6=Sample Band 1 (upper band) = exon 3 included. Band 2 (lower band) = exon 3 skipped (Δ3). Identities were supplied by the experimenter and are used as given. No product sizes are assumed in any calculation.
A7=Absent excluded signal | B7=Super Minigene Only and ScrMOE have no Band 2 row. The experimenter confirmed the exports are complete, so excluded volume is 0 (highlighted in Quantification). A 100% signal fraction does not exclude undetectable skipped transcript.
A8=Export cross-check | B8=Quantification column K compares each computed Ψ with the Band 1 Volume Ratio printed in the export. Differences are limited to rounding of the export's 3-decimal ratio.
A9=Summary | B9=Lane values only. Deltas are Ψ minus the ScrMOE lane and Ψ minus the Super Minigene Only lane, in percentage points. nt start and end come from the ASO labels.
A10=Replication and testing | B10=One gel per ASO, so n = 1: no mean, SD, paired tests or p-values are computed. Numeric exports alone cannot establish PCR linearity, signal saturation or sample provenance.
A11=Cross-gel comparison | B11=The Super Minigene Only and ScrMOE controls are on gel 7-7 only. ASOs F–K (gel 7-9) have no on-gel control, so their deltas compare across gels, which differ in run conditions (band Rf and ladder spacing differ between the two gels). Treat F–K deltas as provisional until a control is run beside them.
A12=Ladder-estimated sizes | B12=For reference only, not used in any calculation: the exports estimate Band 1 at about 548–609 bp and Band 2 at about 286–338 bp, with the two bands about 260–277 bp apart. Estimates shift between gels 7-7 and 7-9.
A13=SMN2 specificity | B13=Product identity rests on the construct-specific primer design used in the experiment.
A14=Exclusions | B14=No reported band rows are dropped. Ladder rows stay in the raw tables and do not enter sample Ψ. Gel 7-7 lane 2 does not appear in the export, so it is not represented.
A15=Raw import | B15=PDF table text parsed into the original columns. Cal.Volume dashes preserved as text. The Cal.Volume entry for ASO K Band 2 (7-9) was blank in the supplied text and is recorded as '-'. Raw 7-7 and Raw 7-9 retain all original values.
A16=Formula storage | B16=Live Excel formulas include cached values, enabling immediate display without recalculation.

