    32	class FormulaReader:
    33	    """Evaluate only arithmetic and cell references; never execute workbook code."""
    34	
    35	    reference = re.compile(r"(?:(?:'([^']+)'|([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9 ]*))!)?(\$?[A-Z]{1,3}\$?\d+)")
    36	
    37	    def __init__(self, workbook):
    38	        self.workbook = workbook
    39	
    40	    def value(self, sheet, coordinate, active=None):
    41	        active = set() if active is None else active
    42	        key = (sheet, coordinate)
    43	        if key in active:
    44	            raise ValueError('cyclic formula reference')
    45	        value = self.workbook[sheet][coordinate].value
    74	| J | 7-9 | 135–152 | 41.622 |
    75	| K | 7-9 | 151–168 | 41.776 |
    76	
    77	All 11 labeled intervals have an internally consistent inclusive length of 18;
    78	that arithmetic does not verify their sequence, strand, or coordinate origin.
    79	Band 1 migrates more slowly and has a larger reported MW than Band 2 in all
    80	11 pairs, consistent with the supplied size order but insufficient to establish
    81	isoform identity. Exported MW proxies range from 547.923–569.977 (Band 1) and
    82	285.788–294.360 (Band 2) on 7-7, versus 587.008–609.070 and 322.032–338.495 on
    83	7-9. Pair separations range from 260.200–277.344 across both gels. These are
    84	**derived ranges of unverified sizing proxies**: both different product lengths
    85	and cross-gel calibration shifts require investigation. Primer-derived expected
    86	sizes are null because neither primer nor construct sequences are present.
    87	No fragment-length correction is applied; integrated signal fractions can differ
    88	from molecular fractions when products have different lengths.
    89	
    90	`needs_human_confirmation` in the JSON and manifest lists the unresolved items:
    91	ASO sequences/orientation/chemistry, construct/version/exon origin, primer binding
    92	sites/expected products, band identities, size shifts, original images/PDFs,
    93	detection limits, experimental-unit lineage and biological/technical replication,
    94	gel 7-9 controls, and coordinate compatibility. Biological and technical replicate
    95	IDs remain separate null fields. Gel/lane identifiers identify measurements only;
    96	they are not assigned either kind of replicate. No mean, SD or error bars are
    97	justified by the workbook's reported n=1.
    98	
    99	Computational comparison: **not comparable**. The assay is reported as a
   100	super-minigene, and construct-to-genome coordinates, assembly, sequence and
   101	strand are unverified. No feature join was attempted.
   102	
   103	Follow-up validation: obtain the complete construct and ordered ASO/primer
   104	sequences; align and verify all binding sites and expected amplicons; confirm
   105	products with junction sequencing and size anchors; inspect original gel images
   106	for background, saturation and detection thresholds; resolve size shifts; repeat
   107	ASOs with independent biological samples and separately identified technical
   108	repeats, randomized gel placement and matched controls on every gel. Establish
   109	assay linearity and a defensible length-correction protocol before quantitative
   110	transcript PSI interpretation. None of these recommendations retroactively
   111	validate the present measurements.

